{
  "concept": "A shallow neural network computes y as a linear combination (weights φ) of hidden units, where each hidden unit h_i is itself a linear function (weights θ_{i0}, θ_{i1}) of the input x passed through an activation — so the θ parameters govern the input-to-hidden transformation and the φ parameters govern the hidden-to-output combination.",
  "figureType": "network_diagram",
  "elements": [
    "input node x (circle, left)",
    "bias node labeled 1 feeding the hidden layer (upper left, orange)",
    "bias node labeled 1 feeding the output y (top, orange)",
    "three hidden unit nodes h_1, h_2, h_3 (circles, center column, each with a small ReLU-like activation glyph)",
    "output node y (circle, right)",
    "orange directed edges from the hidden-layer bias node to each h_i, labeled θ_{10}, θ_{20}, θ_{30}",
    "black directed edges from x to each h_i, labeled θ_{11}, θ_{21}, θ_{31}",
    "black directed edges from each h_i to y, labeled φ_1, φ_2, φ_3",
    "orange directed edge from the output bias node to y, labeled φ_0",
    "arrowheads on all edges indicating left-to-right data flow",
    "panel-style labels distinguishing the clean view and the fully labeled view"
  ],
  "interactions": [
    {
      "id": "selectHiddenUnit",
      "type": "click",
      "teaches": "Each hidden unit h_i owns exactly one slice of the parameterization: its bias θ_{i0}, its input weight θ_{i1}, and its output weight φ_i — clicking a unit isolates the computation y's dependence on that single unit and shows the parameters travel together per neuron",
      "label": "Select hidden unit"
    },
    {
      "id": "labelView",
      "type": "toggle",
      "label": "Diagram view",
      "options": ["Clean (panel b)", "Labeled (panel a)"],
      "default": "Labeled (panel a)",
      "teaches": "The underlying architecture is identical in both views; the labeled view makes the full θ and φ parameter names explicit while the clean view shows the same network stripped down to its structure",
      "default_note": ""
    },
    {
      "id": "hiddenUnitCount",
      "type": "slider",
      "label": "Number of hidden units",
      "range": [1, 6, 1],
      "default": 3,
      "teaches": "The architecture scales by adding hidden units, and each added unit contributes exactly 3 new parameters (θ_{i0}, θ_{i1}, φ_i) — so parameter count grows linearly with hidden-layer width while x and y stay fixed"
    }
  ],
  "demo_steps": [
    {
      "title": "The fully labeled network",
      "narration": "Panel (a) shows every parameter: orange bias connections carry θ_{i0} into each hidden unit and φ_0 into the output, black connections from x carry θ_{i1}, and hidden-to-output connections carry φ_i.",
      "state": { "labelView": "Labeled (panel a)", "hiddenUnitCount": 3 }
    },
    {
      "title": "Trace one hidden unit",
      "narration": "Click h_2: its incoming bias θ_{20}, input weight θ_{21}, and outgoing weight φ_2 light up together — each hidden unit owns exactly these three parameters, a mini linear-model-plus-activation feeding y.",
      "state": { "labelView": "Labeled (panel a)", "hiddenUnitCount": 3 }
    },
    {
      "title": "Same network, clean view",
      "narration": "Toggle to panel (b): the architecture is unchanged, but the weight names are hidden. Switching back and forth confirms the labels are annotation, not structure.",
      "state": { "labelView": "Clean (panel b)", "hiddenUnitCount": 3 }
    },
    {
      "title": "Grow the hidden layer",
      "narration": "Drag the slider to add hidden units: x and y stay fixed while each new unit h_i appears with its own θ_{i0}, θ_{i1}, and φ_i. The network's capacity grows one independent three-parameter unit at a time.",
      "state": { "labelView": "Labeled (panel a)", "hiddenUnitCount": 5 }
    }
  ],
  "keyInsight": "Every hidden unit contributes exactly one self-contained trio of parameters — bias θ_{i0}, input weight θ_{i1}, output weight φ_i — so a shallow network is just a sum of independent per-unit linear models, and widening the layer adds three parameters per unit.",
  "reconstructionNotes": "Left-to-right layered layout: x at mid-left, hidden units stacked vertically in a center column, y at mid-right. Two orange bias nodes labeled 1: one above-left feeding all hidden units, one at top feeding y directly with edge φ_0. Bias-originated edges in orange; all other edges in black; θ labels on input-to-hidden edges, φ labels on hidden-to-output edges, in italic serif math styling positioned near each edge midpoint. Each hidden unit circle contains a small activation-function glyph (short ReLU-style bent line). Clicking a hidden unit should highlight only its own three parameter edges/labels (plus dim the rest of the graph) — the per-unit parameter bundle is the lesson. In clean view, remove all weight labels and optionally the bias label emphasis but keep identical node/edge structure. When the slider changes hidden-unit count, units fan out symmetrically around the vertical center, with h_i labels, θ_{i0}/θ_{i1}/φ_i labels regenerating consistently for each unit."
}

